    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF incoterms 2020? we have a shipment of semiconductors coming from seoul to hamburg and i need to make sure the insurance coverage is handled correctly by the vendor.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is strictly responsible for delivering goods aboard the vessel at the port of shipment, arranging main carriage to the named destination (in this case, Hamburg), and procuring insurance against the buyer's risk. Crucially for semiconductors, while the seller *must* obtain cargo insurance, they do not need to quote insurance costs or pay specific premiums in your transaction; they only need to provide the policy original to you. You must review the policy clause carefully to ensure it covers your specific semiconductor risks, as the minimum coverage is limited and does not automatically include war risks or all contractor and cabotage policies unless explicitly added.\n\n**Important Note**: Even though it is the seller's duty to *arrange* insurance for this route, you should verify the specific coverage limits and exclusions in the final policy document before shipment, as the buyer retains the primary risk until the goods are unloaded at the final destination. If your products are highly sensitive to voltage fluctuations or have high specific risks, you may need to require the vendor to upgrade the standard policy clause beyond the Incoterm minimum.",
